# Games

`games` is the native clean-room terminal arcade from
[`keys-i/tools`](https://github.com/keys-i/tools). The `action` may be `list`,
`info`, or `run`. Choose a `game` for details or play; choose a `format` of
`--plain` or `--json` when listing. An optional unsigned `--seed` reproduces
the randomized setup; elapsed time and input timing remain live.

Interactive games cannot run inside the dashboard output pane. Selecting
`run` shows the exact direct-terminal command. All eleven modes are built into
the Rust binary; no external game, shell, Python process, network service, or
download is involved.

This scripts pack contains only the shared manual and typed UI contract; it
does not duplicate gameplay or argument logic. The prepared `keys-tools` PyPI
package has not been published.
